The fresh non-vacuity test is now valid: the mutated small-input claim builds, then exits 1 with `WarnStuckClaimState` at a final `<k>false</k>` against the demanded `true`. The static audit also found no unsound proof-local equation; the decisive defect is theorem adequacy—there is simply no result-bearing entry theorem for `N >= 2`, and `isPrimeSpec` is never used by a claim.
All dynamic reconstruction, adequacy checks, exhaustive inventory, and the corrected non-vacuity mutation are complete. The remaining work is to consolidate the proven/assumed ledger and issue the required review markers.
